EXT. BRIDGE OVER A BOTTOMLESS RAVINE - DAWN

A rope bridge strung between two cliffs, shrouded in mist. Below, a river roars unseen.

A HOODED TRAVELER (30s, patched cloak, a staff in hand) stands at the near end. On the far side waits a TROLL, ORVAL GRUNDSTONE (towering, mossy, a toll ledger tucked under one arm).

HOODED TRAVELER
Is this the only crossing?

ORVAL
Only one for a hundred leagues.

HOODED TRAVELER
Then I'll pay the toll.

ORVAL
Toll is a story. A true one.

The traveler sets down the staff, lowers the hood to reveal a weathered face and a braid of silver-streaked hair.

HOODED TRAVELER
Very well. My name is Maelis. I was a queen.

ORVAL
Many were.

MAELIS
I lost my crown to my brother.

ORVAL
Many did.

MAELIS
I killed him for it.

Orval stops writing in the ledger. The mist swirls between them.

ORVAL
That is new.

MAELIS
Is it enough?

ORVAL
It is a beginning. Cross. Mind the third plank.

She steps onto the bridge. It sways. She grips the rope.

MAELIS ^
I will mind it.

ORVAL ^
I did not say it was safe.

She crosses, plank by plank, one hand always on the rope. At the third plank she pauses, steps over it, and continues. On the far side, Orval offers a massive hand to help her up. She takes it.

ORVAL (CONT'D)
Your name was Maelis.

MAELIS
It still is.

ORVAL
Is it?

She smiles, thin and tired, and walks on into the mist.
